# Intent: Train 6 item 2, music dance on the unit (legacy patches 100, 101, 121, 124, 126 to 128, 130 and 131 rebuilt as one change on the Train 4 tree). Sound-reactive motion and mood faces. The audio input task hands every chunk it reads from the codec (24 kHz, two channels, before the 16 kHz resampler) to maipai_music_tap, which reads channel 0 only and runs the plain C front end of maipai_music_core.h (four band-pass biquads, a DC blocker, zero crossings, one frame per 20 ms). A low-priority worker (4 KB stack and about 3 KB of history in PSRAM) turns the frames into a few numbers once a second: level, tempo with its confidence, spectral flatness, the share of envelope variance at 3 to 6 Hz (speech), pauses. No audio leaves the unit and none is kept. The tap stands still (and the history is cleared) while the unit listens, speaks or plays a sound and for 1.5 s after, and it is never reached while muted or in full quiet (ReadAudioData returns first, patch 107). With Home reachable the unit sends the numbers as music_feat events (level above 400 only) and the host decides (host music_dance.py). With the link down the unit decides itself with the same judge (maipai_music_judge.h, tested equal to the host's Python judge): four seconds of music is the nod (happy face, head bobs up and down on the beat), 15 s later the dance (the head sways on the song's beat with the Happy squint: BeatSwayModifier, which plays the Happy keyframes when no beat is clear), a dance block of 5 minutes on a charger or 2 on battery, then a 90 s slow mood (the gentle sway goes on), nine seconds without music pauses it and 60 s ends the session; two minutes between sessions. Mood faces (maipai_music_mood_core.h): a calm song keeps the happy face, a middling one swaps happy and laughing every 12 s, a fast loud one laughs; the face is set only when the answer changes. Not while muted, in full quiet, connecting, listening, speaking or upgrading, nor on a battery below 20 percent (a dance needs 40). Tools self.music.set (on or off, saved in its own storage namespace, off until turned on) and self.music.get_status. Left out of the legacy set on purpose: the clip capture for song naming and the notes on the face (they need the host's naming path and a display change), so no audio is ever copied out.
# Placement: unit (the unit dances to music by itself with the host off; with the host on the host decides, as before)
# Upstream: firmware/xiaozhi-esp32/main/audio/audio_service.cc (MIT) for the tap; new files hal/maipai_music.cc, maipai_music_core.h, maipai_music_judge.h, maipai_beat.h, maipai_music_mood_core.h and stackchan/modifiers/beat_sway.h; the head and eye keyframes are those of the StackChan Happy dance (MIT)
# Check after a flash: self.music.get_status answers enabled false and state idle; self.music.set true then play a song at normal volume one metre away with the hub stopped: the happy face after about 5 s, the head bobbing on the beat, the dance after about 20 s, the serial lines "offline music: nod / dance / end" (state in get_status moves nod, dance); start the hub: a running dance stops; the unit's own speech and chimes never start a nod; muted or quiet: nothing; the wake word and chat work as before.
# Kconfig: MAIPAI_MUSIC_DANCE (default y: measured at about 2.3 KB of steady free internal RAM with the other Train 6 patches, under the 4 KB rule; off at run time until self.music.set turns it on, and while off the audio path pays one atomic read per chunk); off compiles out the tap, the worker, the modifier and both tools. See docs/design/train6-2026-11-16.md.
